# LAB4a-uncapped: a game frame for every film frame, stepped as slop steps it (`clock
# free`, `stepping uncapped`). e1m1's first corridor at a run, in the Classic box at
# 1440x1080 with the torches' flicker, gliding lights and smooth motion on, the status bar
# and the gun ("id capped the game"). The run (x 480 from y -352, about 137 units a
# second, 0.25 s ramps, id's bob) lasts all of the film's 6.5 s, swaying 8 degrees either
# way every 2.6 s, so the picture slides sideways and a dropped tick shows. The camera's
# keys are dense (every 1/30 s): the run's speed is integrated, its sway a sine.
#
# Assembly (LAB4a): halves as ST1b's: the central 720 columns of LAB4a-id on the left
# ("ID'S 72 FPS CAP") and of LAB4a-uncapped on the right ("A FRAME EVERY REFRESH"). The
# sound is LAB4a-uncapped's.

map e1m1

duration 8.5
fps 60
size 1440x1080

preset classic
mode 960x600
display 4:3
clock free
stepping uncapped
hud on
gun on
bob on
player camera
cvar gamma 0.8
cvar r_torchflicker 1
cvar r_lerplightstyles 1
cvar r_lerpmove 1
cvar r_lerpmodels 1

camera path
key 0.0000  480,-352.000,110  0,90.000  ease linear
key 0.0333  480,-352.000,110  0,90.000  ease linear
